spans.s:
परापत् परा-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -पति-
तुम्, to fly away, escape; to depart; to fall out;
to fail: Caus. -पातयति, to chase or drive away.

परा-वर्त, अस्, m. turning back, turning round;
retreat; reversal of a sentence; exchange, barter;
restoration.

परा-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, turned back, returned,
fled, retreated; turned round, revolved; exchanged;
reversed (as a judgment); given back, restored.

परा-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck down or back;
driven back, repelled, repulsed; struck, assailed;
driven on; (अम्), n. a stroke.

पारत्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the next world;
rewarded in a future state (according to Kullūka =
परलोक-फल).

पारदेश्य, अस्, शी, अम्, belonging to or coming
from a foreign country, foreign; (अस्), m. a traveller,
one who has gone to a foreign country; a foreigner;
[cf. Lat. per-egrinus.]

पारहंस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पर-हंस), re-
lating to an ascetic who has subdued all his senses;
[cf. पारमहंस्य.]
